<title>SWEDEN: MoDo says to cut 100 jobs in Sweden.</title>
<headline>MoDo says to cut 100 jobs in Sweden.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group MoDo said on Monday its paper division would shed 100 jobs at its Silverdalen mill in Sweden after a change in marketing strategy.</p>
<p>&quot;In the future, sales will be concentrated on markets where the mill has advantages in marketing, delivery and service, i.e. the Nordic region, Great Britain, the Benelux, Russia and the Baltic states,&quot; MoDo said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the measure had been brought about by increased low-price competition from standard coated paper in Central Europe as a consequence of a substantial increase in production capacity.</p>
<p>&quot;The new direction will necessitate an adaptation of production volume and a change in shifts at the mill. In all, the change means that the number of employees must be cut by around 100 people,&quot; MoDo said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
